= Computer science =

== Scope ==
Computer science is the study of computation, information processing, algorithms, programs, computational systems, and the principles and techniques used to represent and solve problems computationally.

== Includes ==
This category includes algorithms and data structures, programming languages, software systems, computer architecture, operating systems, networks, databases, security and cryptography, distributed systems, theory of computation and complexity, human-computer interaction, artificial intelligence/machine learning, graphics, scientific computing, and related computational methods.

== Excludes / boundary ==
Not every use of digital technology is automatically computer science. General consumer technology, electronics, engineering, mathematics, or domain applications belong here only when the computational method/system itself is a defining part of the subject. Cross-domain pages may belong to multiple categories rather than being forced into one branch.

